# Line endings are git's job, not the application's.
#
# This repository is written on Windows, built on Linux, and ships shell
# scripts that run inside a container. A CRLF file crossing that boundary fails
# in ways that read as anything but a line-ending bug -- api/orchestrator.py
# strips \r\n out of every trainer file as it packs the tarball precisely
# because that already happened once, and cost a real run.
#
# That normalisation stays as a second line of defence. This file is the first.
# See ADR-0010.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything executed by a POSIX shell, in a container or on a VM. LF, always.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one thing here that genuinely wants CRLF.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf

# Binary, or generated and not worth reading in a diff.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.ico       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.safetensors binary
uv.lock       -diff linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true
